       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order, even with your confirmation.\n\n- **The dose is dangerous.** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen, and each 1,600 mg dose is twice the maximum single dose. Confirming the order doesn't change that. No prescriber should give this, and I won't enter it for anyone.\n- **This needs to come from a prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician, so a medication order has to come from the patient's treating team.\n\n**What to do next:**\n1. **Call the patient's attending physician or the medicine team.** They can confirm what was meant. It's likely a typo, such as 400 mg four times daily.\n2. **Ask the ward or on-call pharmacist** if you need the dose checked quickly.\n3. **If the patient needs pain relief now,** the bedside nurse can contact the covering physician for an appropriate order.\n\nOnce a prescriber confirms a dose within safe limits, I can help them enter it right away."
      }
